== multiclass
ok   OneVsRestClassifier: per-class estimators equal separate binary fits of class-vs-rest (coef_)
ok   OneVsRestClassifier.predict_proba = per-class P(class) normalised to sum 1 (documented: 'rows sum to 1' in the single-label case)
ok   OneVsRestClassifier.decision_function = stacked binary decision functions; predict = argmax
ok   OneVsRestClassifier multilabel: predict_proba = marginal per-label probabilities (not normalised) and predict = indicator of decision_function > 0
ok   OneVsOneClassifier: pairwise estimators equal separate fits on the class pairs (label 0 for the smaller class)
ok   OneVsOneClassifier.decision_function = votes + sum_of_confidences / (3 (|sum| + 1)) recomputed from the pairwise estimators
ok   OneVsOneClassifier.predict = argmax of that (confidence breaks vote ties without overturning a vote difference of 1)
   OvO: 0 test rows with a full vote tie (1,1,1) -> decided by confidences
   OvO triangle: 2 grid points with cyclic votes (1,1,1); library predictions there [0, 1, 1] per class
ok   OneVsOneClassifier on cyclic-vote points (votes 1,1,1): predict = argmax of the summed confidences (documented confidence tie-break), recomputed from the pairwise fits  (2 tie points)
ok   OutputCodeClassifier(code_size=2): int(n_classes*code_size) = 6 estimators, code_book_ shape (3, 6) in {-1, 1} (estimator has decision_function)
ok   OutputCodeClassifier.predict = class whose code word is nearest (euclidean) to the vector of binary decision_function values
ok   OutputCodeClassifier estimators are binary fits on the code-book columns (constant columns get a constant predictor)  (4 non-constant columns of 6)
ok   OutputCodeClassifier with an estimator lacking decision_function: code_book_ in {0, 1}
